UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This was another hand where careful planning is crucial to making the hand. In general, to plan the hand out you count your winners and figure out a plan to take as many tricks as you need to make your contract. |
PG| ***** 89 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Moreover, you need to be aware of entry issues sometimes such as on this hand. In particular, sometimes suits block, as spades do on this hand.|
PG| ***** 90 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So the best line of play is to play the @SQ immediately to unblock spades, before playing hearts That way there will still be a dummy entry to cash the @SJ. Declarer will then take 3 spade tricks, 3 heart tricks, 3 club tricks, and 1 diamond trick and make 4.|
PG| ***** 91 ***** |


